Mouse Following Insect 🪲

An interactive browser-based insect created using HTML5 Canvas, CSS, and JavaScript.

The insect smoothly follows the user's mouse cursor while its segmented body, legs, wings, and antennae move naturally with it.

✨ Features
🪲 Interactive insect that follows the mouse cursor
🦵 Animated legs and segmented body
🪽 Transparent wings
👀 Animated-looking eyes and antennae
🖱️ Real-time mouse tracking
🎨 Canvas-based rendering
⚡ No external libraries required
🌐 Runs directly in a web browser
🛠️ Technologies Used
HTML5
CSS3
JavaScript
HTML5 Canvas API
🚀 How to Run
Clone this repository:
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPOSITORY.git
Open the project folder.
Open index.html in your browser.

That's it! No installation or dependencies are required.

🎮 How It Works

The project uses the HTML5 Canvas API to draw the insect.

JavaScript tracks the mouse position and continuously updates the insect's position and rotation.

The body is made from multiple segments that follow the segment in front of them, creating a smooth, organic movement.

